Here's your complete guide document! It covers everything you need to build this project step by step. Here's a quick summary of what's inside:

The guide is structured in 9 phases:

Project Setup — Prerequisites (Node, Python, MongoDB, Docker), VSCode extensions to install (including Copilot), and Git initialization
Frontend Setup — All npm packages to install, TailwindCSS config, and exactly which files to create
Backend Setup — All packages, TypeScript config, .env setup, MongoDB models, and a full API endpoint reference table
AI Engine — Python venv setup, all pip packages, how to generate the synthetic 5000-complaint dataset, and how to train your models
Connecting Everything — How Node.js talks to FastAPI, and how React talks to Node
Running Locally — All 4 terminal commands to start MongoDB, backend, AI engine, and frontend + Docker Compose
Key Features with Copilot — Exact Copilot comment prompts to paste for each major feature (map, emergency buttons, AI preview form, admin dashboard)
Testing — Using Thunder Client (built into VSCode) to test all your APIs
Scalability + Checklist — Redis caching, indexes, message queues, and a final verification checklist
Pro tip for Copilot: The guide includes the exact multi-line comment prompts to paste at the top of each file — Copilot will read them and generate most of the code automatically. Follow the Week-by-Week build order table so you always have a working piece before adding the next layer.

