Here's your complete Frontend Development Guide — a step-by-step document with full source code for every single file. Here's what's inside across 12 modules:

Module 1 — Project Init & Config — Vite scaffold, all npm install commands in one block, full tailwind.config.js, index.css with reusable Tailwind component classes, vite.config.ts with proxy, tsconfig.json, and .env

Module 2 — TypeScript Types & Constants — Complete type definitions for Complaint, User, AIClassificationResult, plus EMERGENCY_CONTACTS, STATUS_COLORS, and CATEGORY_ICONS

Module 3 — API Services Layer — Axios base instance with JWT interceptor + 401 redirect, authService, complaintService (with multipart image upload), and analyticsService

Module 4 — Redux State — Full authSlice with async thunks for login/register/loadMe, store/index.ts, useAuth hook, and useGeolocation hook

Module 5 — Common Components — Navbar, StatusBadge, PriorityBadge, Spinner, PageSpinner, Modal

Module 6 — Live Map — Leaflet LiveMap with colored CircleMarker per status, Popup with complaint info, and a MapLegend

Module 7 — Dashboard Components — EmergencyButtons (tap-to-call grid), AreaRiskCard (score gauge), NearbyAlerts (scrollable urgent list)

Module 8 — Complaint Submission — ImageUpload with previews, GPSCapture, EmergencyToggle, AIPreviewCard (shows AI result before submit)

Module 9 — Pages — Full AuthLogin with Zod validation, full CitizenDashboard, full SubmitComplaint with debounced AI preview

Module 10 — Routing — ProtectedRoute with role-based access, full App.tsx with lazy loading, main.tsx with Leaflet icon fix

Module 11 — Admin Analytics — TrendChart (Recharts LineChart), DepartmentRanking (horizontal BarChart), CityHealthScore

Module 12 — Run & Fix — Start command, common errors table with fixes, Copilot tips, and a complete file creation checklist you can tick off in VSCode

When you're ready, say "give the backend guide" and I'll build the same depth guide for the Node.js/Express/MongoDB module.

