==============================================================
  SMART CIVIC PLATFORM — STEP 01: PROJECT INITIALIZATION
==============================================================

BEFORE YOU START — INSTALL THESE ON YOUR MACHINE
-------------------------------------------------
1. Node.js 20 LTS        → https://nodejs.org
2. Python 3.11           → https://python.org
3. MongoDB Community     → https://mongodb.com/try/download/community
4. Git                   → https://git-scm.com
5. Docker Desktop        → https://docker.com/products/docker-desktop

VSCODE EXTENSIONS TO INSTALL (Press Ctrl+Shift+X and search each)
-------------------------------------------------------------------
- GitHub Copilot
- GitHub Copilot Chat
- ESLint
- Prettier - Code formatter
- Tailwind CSS IntelliSense
- Python (Microsoft)
- Pylance
- Thunder Client
- MongoDB for VS Code
- GitLens
- Auto Rename Tag
- Path Intellisense


==============================================================
  PART A — CREATE THE ROOT PROJECT FOLDER
==============================================================

Open VSCode.
Press Ctrl+` to open the terminal.
Run these commands ONE BY ONE:

------------------------------------------------------------
mkdir smart-civic-platform
cd smart-civic-platform
git init
code .
------------------------------------------------------------

This opens a new VSCode window inside smart-civic-platform/.
All future work happens in THIS window.


==============================================================
  PART B — CREATE THE ROOT .gitignore FILE
==============================================================

In VSCode:
  1. Press Ctrl+N to create a new file
  2. Press Ctrl+S and save it as:   .gitignore
     (make sure it is in smart-civic-platform/ root)

PASTE THIS CONTENT into .gitignore:

------------------------------------------------------------
# Node
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.npm

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pkl
venv/
.env
*.egg-info/

# Environment files
.env
.env.local
.env.production

# Logs
*.log
logs/

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db